From 034b662100a905f1305bb566397da7361530223e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 21:59:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] moe cache: sync-free decode device remap for
 --host-experts pinned (GGML_MOE_DEVREMAP)

The eager path reads the routing back to the host before each routed op (one device synchronize per op), runs the
residency policy and uploads the remap.  Here the scheduler offers the input to the backend first (moe_cache_remap
iface, the last member, NULL elsewhere): a kernel maps the device routing through a per-table expert -> slot map
(slots + e = cold, read in place from the pinned master) and writes the routing into mapped pinned memory; the policy
runs on it at the next call and re-uploads the map after a residency change.  One launch serves a layer's tables.
Each expert is read from the same bytes, so the output does not change.  Pinned masters, single slice, no identity
table, not under -sm tensor; the eager path still primes and sizes the cache.  GGML_MOE_DEVREMAP=0: off (the eager
path).
